# Dolarito — environment variables.
# Copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.

# --- Supabase (T002) -------------------------------------------------------
SUPABASE_URL=

# Ingestion writes with this key only. It lives in the GitHub Actions secrets
# and must never reach a browser bundle (constitution Art. V, plan.md 2.3).
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Used only by the negative RLS test in T005: with no anonymous read policy,
# this key must fail both read and write. Not used by the app at runtime.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# --- Web server-side reads (T023) ------------------------------------------
# plan.md 2.3 requires every read to happen server-side with a server key, so
# no credential reaches the browser.
#
# N4, 2026-09-14: ACCEPTED RISK, not resolved. Supabase's dashboard cannot bind
# a key to a Postgres role — every secret key carries elevated access and
# bypasses RLS — so this ends up holding the service_role key, which also
# writes, deletes and does DDL. A compromised web server could empty `quotes`,
# and the captured history is the one irrecoverable thing in this project.
#
# The `web_reader` role exists and is inert, waiting for either Supabase to
# allow key-to-role binding or for reads to move to direct Postgres. See
# plan.md 2.3.
SUPABASE_SERVER_READ_KEY=

# --- Site protection (T022, HU-07) -----------------------------------------
# Shared password for the private period. Removing protection is a config
# change, not a code change.
#
# Three states, and the third one is deliberate:
#
#   a password    the site is gated
#   off           the site is open -- this is the configuration change
#                 HU-07 asks for
#   unset/blank   503: the site serves nothing at all
#
# A missing variable does NOT mean open. The likeliest accident of the
# private period is deploying without setting this, and if that meant open,
# the accident would publish the site silently -- the one thing HU-07 exists
# to prevent. Failing closed costs an outage only the owner ever sees.
#
# Required on Vercel for the T021 deployment. The cookie is an HMAC keyed by
# this value, so changing it signs everyone out: that is the intended way to
# revoke access.
SITE_PASSWORD=

# --- Which route opened the run (T018) -------------------------------------
# Optional, and only meaningful locally. In Actions the workflow sets it from
# the event, so `github_schedule` appears when GitHub's scheduler fires and
# `pg_cron` when the scheduled job dispatches.
#
# Set it to `local` when running `pnpm ingest` by hand. Without it a local run
# writes NULL, which is also what the runs from before the column say — and
# then NULL would mean two different things. Only recognised values are sent;
# anything else is dropped rather than failing the insert.
INGEST_TRIGGER=local

# --- Outbound HTTP identity (T006c, constitution Art. V.4) -----------------
# Honest, identifiable User-Agent with a way to reach us. Never impersonate a
# browser to get around controls.
#
# REQUIRED, and validated at runtime: http.ts refuses to send a request if this
# is missing, carries no URL or email, or still contains the `.invalid`
# placeholder below. Article V is one of the three that do not bend for
# implementation convenience, and an unreachable contact in front of a source is
# exactly what V.4 forbids. Replace the domain with a real one before any
# adapter runs.
INGEST_USER_AGENT="dolarito/0.1 (+https://example.invalid; contact@example.invalid)"
